Subject: [PATCH 5/5] Add the GPT-5.6 Terra fact and its Codex targets

Reason: Codex CLI serves gpt-5.6-terra alongside luna and sol, but the packaged
catalog only records the other two, so Nonoka X's desktop routing has no target
to point at. LOCAL_CODEX rows are deliberately not auto-wired into targets
(AUTO_TARGET_LOCAL_AGENT_PROFILES lists dsh only, because an agent CLI's model
list is the vendor's), so the row has to come with its own completion and
search-entitled targets, exactly as luna and sol do.

quality_score is the owner's grading: 80, between sol's 90 and luna's 70. The
remaining capability columns mirror luna's measured row -- same context and
output window, same thinking ladder -- as the conservative copy of a sibling
in the same family rather than a measurement of terra. Replace them once the
model has been profiled.

Removal: Delete once upstream records terra in the packaged catalog.

